{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"The cause is concrete: object spread is applied left-to-right, so the current `{...local, ...defaults}` writes `timeoutMs: 2500` first and then overwrites it with `5000`. Reversing those two spreads makes defaults the base and lets only supplied local keys replace them; because local has no `endpoint`, the default endpoint remains present."}}
